Thanks — I can help. First, there’s an important data inconsistency we should resolve so the numbers and narrative are accurate.

Runway check (inconsistency)
- You gave: cash = $650K and burn = $158K/month. Runway = cash / burn = 650,000 / 158,000 ≈ 4.11 months.
- But you also wrote 18 months of runway. Those two cannot both be true.
  - If runway is actually 18 months with $650K cash, implied burn = 650,000 / 18 ≈ $36.1K/month.
  - If burn is actually $158K/month and runway must be 18 months, required cash = 158,000 * 18 = $2,844,000.

Please tell me which numbers are correct (cash, burn, and runway), or whether one of them was a projection/target rather than current.

What I can do now
- Explain how to calculate the revenue growth and retention metrics you asked for.
- Provide targets/benchmarks and a concise finance narrative you can use in internal materials.
- If you give me prior-period revenue and/or customer/ARR details (see list below), I’ll compute the exact metrics and draft slide text or a one-page memo.

Revenue growth metrics — formulas and examples
- Quarter-over-Quarter (QoQ) growth = (ThisQuarter - PriorQuarter) / PriorQuarter
  - Example: if prior quarter = $360K, QoQ = (420K - 360K) / 360K = 16.7%
- Year-over-Year (YoY) growth = (ThisQuarter - SameQuarterPriorYear) / SameQuarterPriorYear
- Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) for n periods = (End / Start)^(1/n) - 1
- Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR) growth rate (if you have MRR): MRR growth % = (MRR_this_month - MRR_prev_month) / MRR_prev_month
- Annualize a quarterly run rate: ARR ≈ QTR_revenue * 4 (only reliable if seasonal effects are small)

Retention metrics — definitions, formulas, and a quick example
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (Revenue at start of period — revenue lost to churn/contraction) / Revenue at start
  - Measures ability to keep existing revenue (excludes expansion)
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (Revenue at start + expansion - churn - contraction) / Revenue at start
  - Includes upsells/expansion; NRR >100% indicates expansion more than offsets churn
- Customer churn rate = (Customers lost during period) / (Customers at start of period)
- Revenue churn rate = (Revenue lost from churn / starting revenue)
- Example: Starting cohort revenue = $100K; churn $10K, contraction $5K, expansion $20K
  - GRR = (100K - 10K - 5K) / 100K = 85%
  - NRR = (100K + 20K - 10K - 5K) / 100K = 105%

Benchmarks (broad guidance; vary by industry & customer type)
- Healthy NRR for SaaS/recurring businesses: >100% (best-in-class 110–130% for high expansion models)
- GRR target: >90% is good; <80% is worrying
- Annual revenue churn: <10% is strong for mid-market/enterprise, higher for SMB
- CAC payback: <12 months preferred for fast growth; 12–24 months acceptable for some models
- LTV:CAC >3 is a common target

Key metrics to include in internal materials
- Cash balance, burn, runway (show the math and scenarios)
- Revenue (last quarter, QoQ, YoY), ARR / MRR
- GRR and NRR (and a short explanation)
- Customer count, logo churn, revenue churn
- Gross margin, CAC, CAC payback, LTV, LTV:CAC
- Forecast (next 4 quarters) and scenario sensitivity (baseline / downside / upside)

Suggested finance narrative (short template)
- Opening summary: “As of [date], Northgate Consulting has $650K in cash and a current burn of $158K/month, giving ~4.1 months of runway. Revenue last quarter was $420K.”
  - If you intend to present 18 months runway as a target, state it as such and list the required actions (e.g., reduce burn to $36K/month or raise ~$2.2M).
- Growth story: “Revenue grew X% QoQ / Y% YoY driven by [key product lines, channels, accounts].”
- Retention story: “We maintain a GRR of A% and NRR of B%, driven by [upsell motions, product stickiness], with main leakage coming from [cause].”
- Actions and asks: “To reach 18 months runway / target growth, we recommend: 1) reduce non-core spend by $X/month, 2) accelerate upsell program to lift NRR by Y percentage points, 3) target $Z in bridge financing / ARR expansion.”
- Forecast and KPIs to watch weekly/monthly.

Recommended visuals for slides
- Waterfall: cash -> burn -> runway scenarios (current, cost-cut plan, fundraise)
- Revenue trend line (last 8 quarters or 12 months), QoQ growth % labels
- Cohort retention chart (revenue retention by cohort over time)
- NRR/GRR gauge or table, churn by segment
- Key assumptions & sensitivity table (best/likely/worst case)

What I need from you to compute exact metrics and draft slides/text
- Confirm which of these is correct: cash = $650K, burn = $158K/month, runway = 18 months (or indicate which is a target).
- Prior-period revenue (prior quarter and same quarter prior year)
- Whether revenue is mostly recurring; ARR or MRR if available
- Customer counts at start/end of quarter, expansion revenue and churned revenue (or % churn)
- CAC and gross margin (if you want LTV/CAC and payback computed)

Next steps
- Tell me which numbers to trust (or provide the missing prior-period revenue and retention details). I can then:
  - Calculate QoQ / YoY growth and ARR/MRR,
  - Compute GRR and NRR and churn metrics,
  - Draft a 1-page finance narrative and 3-slide deck outline with speaker notes.

Which data would you like me to start with?

