Thanks — I can help. First, one important data check, then concrete metrics you should show, formulas, what to include in the finance narrative, and next steps I can take for you.

1) Quick data check (inconsistency)
- You gave: cash = $650K, burn = $158K/month, runway = 18 months, revenue last quarter = $420K.
- Monthly revenue = $420K / 3 = $140K/month.
- If burn = $158K/month (gross cash outflow) and revenue = $140K/month, net cash burn = 158K − 140K = $18K/month → runway = 650K / 18K ≈ 36 months.
- If runway truly is 18 months, net burn must be ≈ 650K / 18 ≈ $36.1K/month. With revenue = $140K that implies gross burn ≈ 176.1K/month (not 158K).
Please confirm which definition you used for “burn” (gross burn vs net burn), and whether the 18 months runway already factors in expected revenue or funding.

2) Key revenue-growth metrics to compute and present (with formulas)
- MRR (monthly recurring revenue) = quarterly revenue / 3 = $420K / 3 = $140K (if revenue is recurring).
- ARR (annual run-rate) = last quarter * 4 = $420K * 4 = $1.68M.
- QoQ growth rate = (this quarter − prior quarter) / prior quarter. (Need prior-quarter revenue.)
- YoY growth rate = (this quarter − same quarter last year) / same quarter last year.
- CAGR (multi-period growth) = (ending / starting)^(1/years) − 1.
If you only have one quarter, show run-rate and state you need prior-period data for growth rates.

3) Key retention metrics (definitions and formulas)
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (Starting ARR − churned revenue) / Starting ARR. Measures how much recurring revenue you kept excluding expansions.
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (Starting ARR + expansion − churn − contraction) / Starting ARR. If >100% you’re growing from existing customers.
- Customer churn (logo churn) = number of customers lost during period / customers at start of period.
- Dollar churn = $ revenue lost from churned customers / starting revenue.
- Cohort retention: track cohorts by month/quarter to see retention curve over time.
- Average revenue per customer (ARPC) and expansion rate per customer.
- LTV = gross margin * (ARPC / churn rate) — shorthand; use cohort-derived lifetime where possible.
- CAC payback = CAC / monthly gross margin per customer.

4) Which metrics to show on slides / one-pager
- Executive KPIs: cash, runway (show assumptions), ARR / MRR, QoQ & YoY growth, NRR, GRR, logo churn, ARPC, CAC, LTV, gross margin, burn breakdown (fixed vs variable).
- Cash waterfall / monthly burn chart showing revenue vs expenses vs net burn.
- Cohort retention chart (3–12 months).
- Scenario table: base / conservative / aggressive — show revenue, burn, runway, fundraising need.
- Risks & mitigants (top 3 each).

5) Example finance narrative (short)
Current state — As of today, Northgate Consulting has $650K in cash and a trailing-quarter revenue of $420K (run-rate $1.68M ARR). Based on the numbers you provided there appears to be [an X-month runway — TBD after you confirm burn definition]. Revenue coverage of expenses is near breakeven (monthly revenue ~$140K vs gross burn $158K), so small improvements in retention, pricing, or client expansion materially extend runway. Primary growth levers: (1) upsell/expansion to existing clients (focus on increasing NRR), (2) accelerate new bookings from top 20 prospects, (3) tighten discretionary spend to reduce gross burn. Key ask: define the desired runway target and whether you plan to raise capital in the next 6–12 months.

6) Suggested charts and wording for slides
- Slide 1: Snapshot — cash, runway (explicit assumptions), ARR, QoQ growth, NRR.
- Slide 2: Revenue vs Burn (monthly) — show gross burn, revenue, net burn.
- Slide 3: Retention/cohort analysis — 3-month retention curve and NRR figure.
- Slide 4: Scenario analysis — Base/Conservative/Aggressive with funding need and timing.
- Slide 5: Asks & next steps.

7) Quick actionable items I can do for you right now
- Reconcile runway: I can calculate exact runway under three methods (gross-burn runway, net-burn runway, and projected runway including expected revenue growth) if you confirm whether burn is gross or net and provide prior-quarter revenue.
- Build a one-page finance memo or a 5-slide deck with the charts and narratives above — tell me format (memo or slides) and which scenario assumptions to use.
- Compute retention metrics or run cohort analysis if you can upload or paste the customer revenue / churn data for past quarters/months.

What would you like me to do next? (e.g., reconcile runway using a specific definition, build the 5-slide deck, or compute NRR/GRR if you share historical numbers.)

