Thanks — I can help. First, a quick data check, then calculations, suggested KPIs & formulas you should show, a short finance narrative draft you can use, and next steps/questions.

1) Quick data consistency check
- You gave: cash = $650,000; burn = $158,000/month; revenue last quarter = $420,000.
- Monthly revenue = $420,000 / 3 = $140,000/month.
- With those numbers there are two straightforward runway calculations:
  - Runway if you stop generating revenue (i.e., cash only covering expenses): 650,000 / 158,000 ≈ 4.1 months.
  - Runway assuming last-quarter revenue continues (net burn = expenses − revenue): net burn = 158,000 − 140,000 = $18,000/month → runway = 650,000 / 18,000 ≈ 36.1 months.
- These two results conflict with your stated "18 months runway." That implies one of these is true:
  - Your 18-month runway assumption includes additional future revenue growth, cost cuts, or fundraising; or
  - The 18-month figure is calculated differently (e.g., uses committed revenue, adjusted burn, or a conservative scenario); or
  - One of the input numbers (cash, burn, or revenue) is misstated.

Please confirm which assumption you use for “runway” (cash-only, current revenue continuing, or a forecasted scenario), or share the forecasted assumptions so I can align metrics.

2) Immediate useful calculations (based on provided numbers)
- Monthly revenue (MR) = 420,000 / 3 = $140,000.
- Net burn = Burn − MR = 158,000 − 140,000 = $18,000/month.
- Breakeven revenue per month (to cover current burn) = $158,000 → uplift needed from current MR = (158k − 140k) / 140k ≈ 12.9% increase in revenue.
- Runway scenarios:
  - No revenue: 650k / 158k ≈ 4.1 months.
  - Current revenue repeating: 650k / 18k ≈ 36.1 months.
  - To get runway = 18 months with current cash, acceptable net burn = 650k / 18 ≈ $36,111/month → that implies you could be burning ~36k/month (worse than current 18k), so your stated 18 months is inconsistent unless you mean something else—please clarify.

3) Revenue growth metrics to prepare / track (what to compute & why)
- Quarterly revenue growth (QoQ) = (Rev_this_quarter − Rev_last_quarter) / Rev_last_quarter.
  - Need previous-quarter revenue to compute.
- Year-over-year (YoY) growth = (Rev_this_quarter − Rev_same_quarter_last_year) / Rev_same_quarter_last_year.
- Compound quarterly growth rate (Cqgr) or CAGR over multiple quarters.
- Run-rate / ARR (annualized): ARR = last 3-month revenue * 4 (or monthly MR * 12) — useful for investors.
- MRR growth (if subscription): new MRR, expansion MRR, churned MRR, net new MRR.

4) Retention metrics (definitions, formulas, how to compute)
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (Revenue from existing customers at end of period excluding expansions) / (Revenue from same customers at start). Shows how much of baseline revenue you keep.
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (Revenue from same customer base at end including expansions/contractions) / (Revenue from same customers at start). NRR >100% means expansion offsets churn.
- Logo churn rate = (# customers lost during period) / (# customers at start of period).
- Revenue churn rate = (Revenue lost from churned customers during period) / (Revenue at start of period).
- Cohort retention: track cohorts by month/quarter; measure % revenue remaining after 1, 3, 6, 12 months.
- To compute these you need customer-level or cohort revenue data (start revenue by customer/cohort and end revenue by the same group).

5) KPIs to include in internal financial materials
- Liquidity & runway: cash, burn, net burn, runway under scenarios (no revenue, current revenue, projected revenue growth).
- Revenue: Q revenue, QoQ growth, YoY growth, ARR or TTM revenue.
- Margins: gross margin, contribution margin.
- Retention: GRR, NRR, revenue churn, logo churn.
- Sales efficiency: CAC, payback period, LTV, LTV:CAC.
- Pipeline & conversion metrics: sales pipeline value, win rate, average deal size, sales cycle length.
- Operational: utilization rate, professional services backlog (for a consulting firm), average project size, days sales outstanding (DSO).
- Scenario KPIs: sensitivity of runway to +/-10% revenue or +/-10% cost changes.

6) Sample finance narrative (short, internal)
- Executive summary (1–2 sentences): "As of [date], Northgate has $650K in cash and generated $420K in revenue last quarter (MR = $140K). With current operating spend of $158K/month, our net burn is ~$18K/month, giving us ~36 months of runway if revenue continues at Q4 levels. However, if revenue falls or is non-recurring, runway drops to ~4 months on a cash-only basis. We recommend framing scenarios (conservative, base, optimistic) in investor and board materials and highlighting retention/expansion plans to de-risk runway."
- Key drivers & actions:
  - "Close the 12.9% QoQ revenue uplift needed to hit breakeven this month; prioritize high-probability upsell and renewal opportunities."
  - "Focus on reducing client churn and increasing average project size; target NRR >100% through account expansion."
  - "Monitor pipeline and prepare a contingency plan if committed revenue < X over the next 6 months."

7) Suggested visuals for the materials
- Runway sensitivity chart (x-axis: months; lines for no revenue / current revenue / +X% growth scenarios).
- Revenue trend (last 4–8 quarters) with QoQ % labels.
- Cohort retention chart (monthly or quarterly cohorts).
- Waterfall showing revenue changes: New, Expansion, Contraction, Churn.
- KPI dashboard: cash, burn, net burn, runway, ARR, NRR, GRR.

8) Quick recommended next steps / actions I can do for you
- Confirm whether revenue is recurring (subscription/retainers) or project-based.
- Tell me if the 18-month runway includes projected revenue/cost changes or fundraising assumptions.
- If you want, I can:
  - Build a short slide (3–5 slides) with the numbers and charts above (I can draft the text and data sections here).
  - Produce scenario tables showing runway under different growth or cost-cut scenarios.
  - Draft the finance narrative for your board packet or an internal email summarizing findings.

Which of the next steps would you like me to do now? If you want scenario modeling or a slide draft, tell me which scenarios to include (e.g., conservative = no revenue growth, base = flat revenue, optimistic = +10% QoQ growth), and whether revenue is recurring.

