  MRR = Quarterly revenue / 3 (or sum of monthly recurring revenue)
- Gross margin on services
- Customer churn (count) and revenue churn (dollars)
  Customer churn % (monthly) = Customers lost in period / Customers at start of period
  Revenue churn % = Revenue lost from churned/down-graded customers / Revenue at period start
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR)
  GRR = (Revenue at period start − Revenue lost from churn/contraction) / Revenue at period start
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR)
  NRR = (Revenue at period start − churned revenue + expansion revenue) / Revenue at period start
- ARPA / ARPU (average revenue per account / user)
- LTV (lifetime value) and CAC (customer acquisition cost), CAC payback
  LTV ≈ ARPA * Gross margin / churn rate (annualized)
  CAC payback = CAC / (monthly ARPA * gross margin)
- Burn rate, runway, and burn multiple
  Runway (months) = Cash on hand / Net burn per month
  Burn multiple = Cash burn over 12 months / Net new ARR (useful for investors)

