Thanks — I can help. First a quick check on the numbers you gave, then metrics, formulas you can use, a short finance narrative template you can drop into internal materials, and next steps I can take for you.

1) Quick check / important inconsistency
- You said: cash = $650K, burn = $158K/month, runway = 18 months.
- If "burn" is gross operating burn and revenue offsets that, we should use net burn (expenses − revenue) to calculate runway.
- Using your revenue last quarter = $420K → monthly revenue ≈ $420K / 3 = $140K.
  - Net burn = gross burn − monthly revenue = $158K − $140K = $18K/month.
  - That implies runway = 650K / 18K ≈ 36.1 months (not 18 months).
- If runway really is 18 months, the implied net burn would be 650K / 18 ≈ $36.1K/month → which would imply gross burn ≈ revenue + net burn = 140K + 36.1K ≈ $176.1K/month (i.e., higher than $158K).
- Conclusion: either (a) "burn" or "runway" as you reported uses different definitions (gross vs net), or (b) the $420K last quarter is non-recurring / not fully counted in runway, or (c) planned future spend will increase burn. Tell me which definition you use (gross vs net burn) and whether the $420K is sustainable recurring revenue.

2) Key metrics and formulas (you can compute these now or I can compute if you give me the missing numbers)
- Monthly revenue = quarter revenue / 3. (You: $140K/month)
- ARR (if recurring) = monthly revenue × 12 = $140K × 12 = $1.68M.
- Gross burn = total monthly cash outflows (salaries, rent, SaaS, etc.).
- Net burn = gross burn − cash receipts (monthly revenue) = how much cash you lose per month.
- Runway (months) = cash on hand / net burn.
- Quarter-over-quarter (QoQ) growth = (this quarter − prior quarter) / prior quarter.
- Year-over-year (YoY) growth = (this quarter − same quarter last year) / same quarter last year.
- Logo churn rate (count) = customers lost / customers at start of period.
- Revenue churn rate = revenue lost from churned customers / revenue at start of period.
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (revenue at start − revenue lost from churn) / revenue at start.
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (revenue at start − churn + expansions + reactivations) / revenue at start.
- LTV ≈ average revenue per customer × gross margin / customer churn rate.
- CAC payback = cost to acquire a customer / gross margin contribution per month.

