2) Key revenue & retention metrics to compute and include (with formulas)
- Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR) and Annual Recurring Revenue (ARR)
  - MRR = revenue per month (for SaaS-subscription context)
  - ARR = MRR * 12 or annualized trailing revenue (e.g., last 4 quarters)
- Revenue growth
  - Quarter-over-quarter (QoQ) growth = (This Q − Prior Q) / Prior Q
  - Year-over-year (YoY) growth = (This Q − Same Q Last Year) / Same Q Last Year
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR)
  - GRR = (Revenue at start of period from existing customers still retained, excluding expansion) / Starting revenue from those customers
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR)
  - NRR = (Revenue at end of period from the same cohort including expansion − contraction) / Starting revenue for that cohort
- Churn
  - Dollar churn = Lost revenue from churned customers / starting revenue
  - Logo churn = Customers lost / starting customers
- LTV (Customer Lifetime Value)
  - If monthly churn rate = c, ARPA = avg revenue per account monthly, gross margin% = m:
    - LTV ≈ (ARPA * m) / c  (use monthly units consistently)
- CAC and payback
  - CAC = total acquisition cost / new customers acquired
  - CAC payback (months) = CAC / (ARPA * gross margin)
- Unit economics / contribution margin
  - Contribution = revenue − direct variable costs; convert to % of revenue
- Runway sensitivity
  - Show runway under multiple scenarios: current net burn, 10–25% reduction in spend, 10–20% revenue growth, combined scenarios

