I can help — but first a quick clarification because the numbers as given don’t all line up.

Quick checks / immediate calculations
- Monthly revenue = $420,000 / 3 = $140,000.
- You reported burn rate $158,000/month and cash $650,000.
  - If “burn rate” means net cash burn (expenses minus revenue) = $158K/month → runway = 650,000 / 158,000 ≈ 4.1 months.
  - If $158K is gross expenses and revenue is $140K/month → net cash burn = 158K − 140K = $18K/month → runway = 650,000 / 18,000 ≈ 36.1 months.
  - If runway is truly 18 months, implied net burn = 650,000 / 18 ≈ $36.1K/month. With revenue = $140K/month that implies gross expenses ≈ 176.1K/month.

Please confirm which interpretation is correct (is the $158K net or gross burn? Is the 18‑month runway current or projected under some assumptions?), and whether the $420K is recognized revenue (GAAP/ARR style) or bookings/one-time.

What I can do next (pick one)
- Compute accurate runway, scenarios, and cash projection models (best/worst/base) given your assumptions.
- Calculate revenue growth rates and produce YoY / QoQ / MoM growth metrics if you provide prior-period revenue figures.
- Calculate retention metrics (logo churn, dollar churn, gross & net revenue retention) if you give customer counts, MRR/ARR by cohort, and churn.
- Produce investor-ready narrative bullets and a one-page summary or slide text.

Key metrics — formulas and how to calculate them from your data
- Monthly revenue (MRR) = quarterly revenue / 3 = $140K (you have this).
- ARR ≈ last 12 months revenue × (if recurring): sum of last 4 quarters or MRR × 12.
- QoQ growth rate = (this quarter − prior quarter) / prior quarter.
- MoM growth rate = (this month − prior month) / prior month (or use compounded monthly growth rate).
- Logo churn rate = (customers lost during period) / (customers at period start).
- Dollar churn (gross revenue churn) = (MRR lost from downgrades + churned customers) / MRR at period start.
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (MRR at period end from existing customers, including upsells and downgrades) / (MRR at period start) — expresses retention + expansion.
- CLTV ≈ (ARPA / monthly churn) × gross margin (or more detailed lifetime revenue formula).
- CAC payback = CAC / (monthly gross margin per customer).

Suggested KPIs to gather (so we can compute concrete numbers)
- Current customer count, new customers last quarter, lost customers last quarter
- MRR or ARR breakdown by cohort
- Average revenue per account (ARPA)
- Gross margin %, CAC, and churn % (monthly or quarterly)
- Any planned cost changes or expected revenue ramp assumptions

Actionable analysis I can run immediately if you confirm details
- Reconcile runway under three scenarios (current burn, expense cuts, revenue growth scenarios).
- Compute NRR & gross retention with your cohort data (I’ll show how much revenue is at risk).
- Produce a short “finance narrative” (3–5 bullet investor version + 3–5 bullet internal exec version) that emphasizes growth, retention, unit economics, and the runway ask.

Sample investor-safe narrative (template you can adapt)
- “Northgate Consulting generated $420K revenue last quarter (~$140K/mo). Over the last quarter we’ve achieved [X%] revenue growth and maintain [Y%] net revenue retention driven by upsells in [segment].”
- “Current cash is $650K, implying [4 / 18 / 36] months of runway under current assumptions; we’re executing [cost optimization / pricing / upsell] initiatives to extend runway to 12–18 months while pursuing [targeted growth].”
- “Our focus for the next 3 quarters: increase NRR by [target]% through account expansion, reduce CAC via [channels], and improve gross margin through [service mix / pricing].”

Next step
Tell me:
1) Which interpretation of burn/runway is correct (is $158K net or gross?), or whether the 18 months is a forecasted runway under changes.
2) Do you have prior-quarter revenue and basic customer counts / churn? Or should I build scenario models using assumptions?
3) What’s the audience and deadline (board, investors, internal finance deck)?

Once you confirm, I’ll run the specific calculations and prepare the growth & retention metrics plus a concise finance narrative and scenarios.

