Key revenue-growth metrics (what to compute and why)
- Quarter-over-Quarter (QoQ) growth = (ThisQuarter - PriorQuarter) / PriorQuarter
  - Shows recent momentum
- Year-over-Year (YoY) growth = (ThisQuarter - SameQuarterLastYear) / SameQuarterLastYear
  - Shows seasonal/longer-term trend
- Annualized Run Rate = LastQuarterRevenue × 4
  - Quick view of where revenue would land if current quarter repeats
- Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) over N periods = (End / Start)^(1/N) - 1
  - Use for multi-quarter/year trends
- Growth decomposition: New revenue vs. expansion (upsell) vs. churned/contraction revenue
  - Helps explain drivers

Key retention metrics (definitions, formulas, why they matter)
- Customer Retention Rate (by count) = (Customers_end - NewCustomers_added) / Customers_start
  - Measures whether you keep clients
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (Starting_period_revenue - Churned_revenue) / Starting_period_revenue
  - If high, your base is stable (no expansion included)
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (Starting_revenue + Expansion_revenue - Churn - Contraction) / Starting_revenue
  - NRR >100% = growth from existing customers; very important for recurring businesses
- Revenue Churn Rate = Churned_revenue / Starting_revenue (period)
- Logo churn (by customers) = Lost_customers / Starting_customers
- For services/consulting, consider: repeat engagement rate, renewal rate, utilization %, average project size and frequency

Benchmarks (rough, depends on business model)
- SaaS: NRR:
  - Best-in-class: >120%
  - Good: 100–120%
  - Concerning: <100%
- Consulting/services: repeat revenue / retained clients > 60–70% is healthy; utilization > 70–80% depending on model
- Growth targets depend on stage — early-stage startups often target 20%+ QoQ growth; established businesses target lower but sustainable rates.

