- ARR (annualized revenue): $420,000 × 4 = $1,680,000

Runway interpretations:
- If “burn rate” is net burn (i.e., after revenue): runway = cash / net burn = 650,000 / 158,000 ≈ 4.1 months.
- If “burn rate” is gross cash outflow and revenue offsets it (net burn = burn − revenue): net burn = 158,000 − 140,000 = $18,000/month → runway = 650,000 / 18,000 ≈ 36.1 months.
- If the stated runway of 18 months is correct, the implied net burn would be 650,000 / 18 ≈ $36,111/month. That implies revenue is offsetting gross burn by ~158,000 − 36,111 ≈ $121,889/month (i.e., quarterly revenue ≈ $365,667), which is inconsistent with the $420k you reported.

Action: please confirm whether your 158k burn is gross or net, and whether the $420k is recognized revenue for the same period you used to calculate burn/runway. With that we can pick the right baseline.

2) Key revenue-growth metrics to track (definitions + formulas)
- Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR) or average monthly revenue = quarterly revenue / 3 (you have $140k/month).
- ARR = MRR × 12 (or quarter × 4). You: $1.68M ARR.
- Quarter-over-Quarter (QoQ) growth = (This quarter revenue − Prior quarter revenue) / Prior quarter revenue.
- Month-over-Month (MoM) growth = (This month MRR − Prior month MRR) / Prior month MRR.
- CAGR (for longer-term trends).
- New revenue vs. expansion revenue vs. churn/ contraction revenue (needed for NRR).

3) Key retention metrics (definitions + formulas)
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (Starting revenue from existing customers − revenue lost to churn/contraction) / Starting revenue.
  - Shows how much base revenue you keep, excluding upsells.
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (Starting revenue + expansion − contraction − churn) / Starting revenue.
  - >100% NRR means expansion outweighs churn — best indicator of land-and-expand success.
- Logo churn (customer count churn) = #customers lost / starting #customers.
- Revenue churn rate = revenue lost from churn / starting revenue.
- Cohort retention analysis: track the revenue retention of a cohort by month/quarter after acquisition (very useful for consulting retainers vs one-off projects).

Suggested benchmark targets (consulting/services context — adjust by business model):
- Gross retention ≥ 85–95% (higher for recurring services/retainers).
- Net revenue retention ≥ 100–120% (strong sign of expansion).
- MoM MRR growth target: depends on stage — 3–10% MoM for rapid growth stage, 1–3% for steady scaling.
- Logo churn ideally < 5–10% annually for long-term retainer clients.

