4) Retention metrics to include (definitions + targets)
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (Starting ARR − Churned ARR) / Starting ARR
  - Measures revenue kept from existing customers excluding expansion. Healthy target: ≥ 90% (industry dependent).
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (Starting ARR − Churned ARR + Expansion − Contraction) / Starting ARR
  - Includes upsells/expansions. Target: > 100% (best-in-class SaaS), or at least > 95% for many B2B.
- Customer Churn Rate = Customers lost / Customers at start period
  - Monthly churn target depends on model; for subscription B2B keep < 3–5% monthly, better <1.5% for mature.
- Cohort retention curve (month 1, month 3, month 6, month 12) — gives insight into long-term retention.
- LTV (Customer Lifetime Value) = Avg revenue per customer per period × (1 / churn rate) × gross margin
- CAC and LTV:CAC ratio — target LTV:CAC ≥ 3x generally desirable.

