2) Revenue growth metrics — what to calculate and how
- Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR) if applicable:
  - MRR = quarterly revenue / 3 = $140K (from your quarter)
  - ARR = MRR × 12 = $1.68M
- Quarter-over-Quarter (QoQ) growth:
  - QoQ% = (This quarter − Prior quarter) / Prior quarter × 100
  - Example: if prior quarter was $360K, QoQ = (420−360)/360 = 16.7%
- Year-over-Year (YoY) growth:
  - YoY% = (This quarter − Same quarter last year) / Same quarter last year × 100
- Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) for multi-period:
  - CAGR = (Ending Revenue / Starting Revenue)^(1/years) − 1
- Tip: show both quarterly and trailing-12 (TTM) growth to smooth seasonality.

3) Retention metrics — definitions and formulas
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR):
  - GRR = (Starting ARR from existing customers − Revenue lost from churn and downgrades) / Starting ARR
  - Shows how much existing revenue you keep excluding expansion.
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR or NDR):
  - NRR = (Starting ARR + Expansion revenue − Churned revenue − Contraction revenue) / Starting ARR
  - NRR > 100% means expansion offsets churn (powerful growth signal).
  - Example: If Starting ARR = $1.68M, churn = 5% (84K), expansions = 10% (168K) → NRR = (1.68M − 84K + 168K) / 1.68M = 1.05 = 105%
- Customer churn rate (by count):
  - Churn% = (# customers lost during period) / (# customers at start of period)
- Revenue churn rate:
  - Revenue churn% = (Revenue lost to churn during period) / (Starting revenue)
- Other useful retention-related metrics:
  - Expansion rate (upsells)
  - Contraction rate
  - Average revenue per account (ARPA / ARPU)
  - LTV (lifetime value) and CAC payback

