3) Retention metrics to compute (formulas + data needed)
- Starting MRR (or starting ARR for the quarter) — call this S.
- Churned MRR (lost revenue from cancellations) — call this C.
- Expansion MRR (upsells, cross-sells) — call this E.
- Contraction MRR (downgrades) — call this D.

Key formulas:
- Logo churn rate (by customers) = (Customers lost during period) / (Customers at start of period)
- Revenue churn rate = C / S
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (S − C − D) / S  (shows revenue retained from existing customers, excluding expansion)
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (S + E − C − D) / S  (shows overall revenue change including expansion)
- Dollar churn = sum of revenue lost from churned customers

