  - Monthly Revenue (or MRR) trend and seasonality
  - Revenue by stream (retainer/consulting/project/licensing)
- Retention metrics
  - Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (Starting revenue from existing customers − lost revenue) / starting revenue. Target: 90%+ annually for consulting / services
  - Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (Starting revenue + expansion − churn − contraction) / starting revenue. Target: ≥100% is ideal (shows expansion more than churn)
  - Logo churn (clients lost) and revenue churn (dollar churn)
  - Cohort retention & repeat purchase rate (by client cohort month/quarter)
- Unit economics (if applicable)
  - ARPA (avg revenue per account/client)
  - Customer acquisition cost (CAC) and CAC payback
  - LTV (customer lifetime value) = ARPA × gross margin / churn rate
  - LTV : CAC ratio (target 3:1+ for healthy growth)

Quick examples & scenarios
