Thanks — I can help. First, a quick clarification is needed because the numbers you gave are inconsistent unless we know how you define “burn rate” and “runway.” Below I show the possible interpretations and the calculations, then list the key revenue-growth and retention metrics to prepare and next steps I recommend.

1) Quick math / inconsistency check
- Cash on hand = $650,000
- Revenue last quarter = $420,000 → average monthly revenue = 420,000 / 3 = $140,000

Three interpretations:
A. Burn rate = net burn (expenses minus revenue) = $158,000/month
- Runway = cash / net burn = 650,000 / 158,000 ≈ 4.11 months
B. Burn rate = gross operating spend = $158,000/month
- Net burn = gross spend − revenue = 158,000 − 140,000 = $18,000/month
- Runway = 650,000 / 18,000 ≈ 36.1 months
C. Runway = 18 months is fixed (as you stated) with cash = 650,000
- Implied net burn = 650,000 / 18 ≈ $36,111/month
- Implied gross operating spend = revenue + net burn = 140,000 + 36,111 ≈ $176,111/month

Please confirm which interpretation is correct (is the $158K gross expenses or net burn?) or whether the 18 months runway should be treated as a target rather than current.

2) Key revenue growth metrics to prepare (what to compute and show)
- Monthly revenue (MRR equivalent for services) and trailing-12-month (TTM) revenue.
- Quarter-over-quarter (QoQ) growth rate: (Q_current − Q_prior) / Q_prior.
- Year-over-year (YoY) growth (if you have prior-year quarters).
- Compound quarterly or annual growth rates (CAGR) for trend slides.
- Revenue composition: new business vs. expansion vs. one-time.
- Pipeline conversion rates (opportunities → wins) and sales cycle length.

3) Key retention metrics to prepare (definitions + formulas)
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (revenue from existing customers at period end excluding expansions) / (revenue from those customers at period start). Good indicator of churn without expansion.
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (starting revenue + expansions − contractions − churn) / starting revenue. NRR >100% signals expansion offsets churn.
- Customer (logo) churn rate = lost customers / starting customers in period.
- Revenue churn rate = lost revenue / starting revenue in period.
- Cohort retention (month- or quarter-based): survival curve of cohorts over time.
- ARPA / ARPU (average revenue per account) and expansion revenue per account.
- LTV (lifetime value) and CAC (customer acquisition cost) — if you have acquisition spend, compute LTV:CAC and payback months.

4) Benchmarks / targets (general guidance)
- For a services/consulting firm: aim for GRR > 90%, NRR ≥ 100% (if you can drive upsells), logo churn low (<10% annually ideally), and an improving QoQ growth trajectory. Targets vary by business model — tell me if you want industry-specific benchmarks.

5) Suggested finance narrative structure (short)
- Start with the headline: cash, runway, last-quarter revenue, and growth trend.
- Explain the burn/runway context (is current run rate sustainable?).
- Call out retention performance: GRR / NRR / churn — emphasize strengths (e.g., high NRR) or explain mitigation if churn is rising.
- Outline near-term actions: cost optimization, pricing changes, upsell/expansion plans, and fundraising timeline (if needed).
- Close with 3 scenarios (base, optimistic, downside) with expected runway and required actions.

6) Practical next steps I can do for you (pick one or more)
- I can compute QoQ / YoY growth and retention metrics if you provide prior quarter revenue(s) and customer counts/revenue by cohort.
- I can build three financial scenarios (base / hire & growth / conservative) showing runway and headcount/expense implications.
- I can draft the internal finance memo or an investor slide (one-pager) with headline metrics and talking points.
- I can draft an email to the exec team summarizing findings (I will save as a draft unless you tell me to send).

Which do you want next? If you want calculations now, please confirm:
- Whether $158K is net burn or gross expenses (or give monthly expenses).
- Whether the 18 months runway is current fact or a target.
- Prior-quarter revenue (or last 4 quarters) and customer counts / MRR by cohort if available.

