Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
I can help — below I’ll (1) convert the numbers you gave into useful metrics, (2) point out a data discrepancy to reconcile, (3) list the retention and growth metrics you should calculate (with formulas and examples), and (4) give a concise “finance narrative” draft and recommended next steps and slide content you can use in internal materials.

1) Quick conversions from the numbers you gave
- Cash: $650,000
- Last quarter revenue: $420,000 → average monthly revenue = 420,000 / 3 = $140,000/month
- Stated burn rate: $158,000/month
- Stated runway: 18 months

Check/evidence of inconsistency
- If burn rate ($158K) is gross operating spend and revenue reduces cash burn, then net cash burn = 158K − 140K = $18,000/month → implied runway = 650K / 18K ≈ 36 months (not 18).
- If the $158K is net burn (i.e., cash outflow after revenue), runway = 650K / 158K ≈ 4.1 months (not 18).
- If runway = 18 months is correct, implied net burn = 650K / 18 ≈ $36,111/month. That would imply gross burn ≈ net burn + revenue = 36,111 + 140,000 = ≈ $176,111/month (not $158K).

Conclusion: definitions need reconciling. Which of these are you using: is the $158K gross expenses or net cash burn? Is the 18-month runway based on current revenue or an assumed future change?

2) Key revenue-growth and retention metrics to compute (with formulas)
I’ll list the metric, formula, and what you need to compute it.

- Monthly Recurring Revenue (MRR)
  - If you have recurring revenue, MRR = sum of monthly subscription revenue (or quarterly revenue / 3 if all recurring).
  - From your quarter: MRR ≈ $140K (assuming recurring).

- Annual Recurring Revenue (ARR)
  - ARR = MRR × 12
  - Using current MRR: ARR ≈ 140K × 12 = $1,680,000

- Quarter-over-Quarter (QoQ) revenue growth %
  - QoQ growth = (Revenue_this_quarter − Revenue_prev_quarter) / Revenue_prev_quarter × 100%
  - Need previous quarter revenue to compute.

- Year-over-Year (YoY) growth %
  - YoY growth = (Revenue_this_quarter − Revenue_same_quarter_last_year) / Revenue_same_quarter_last_year × 100%
  - Need last-year same-quarter revenue.

- Net Burn (monthly)
  - Net burn = Gross cash outflows (expenses) − cash inflows from operations (revenue)
  - Example with your numbers if gross burn = 158K: net burn = 158K − 140K = $18K/month.

- Runway (months)
  - Runway = Cash on hand / Net burn per month
  - Example: with net burn 18K → runway ≈ 36 months. With net burn 158K → runway ≈ 4.1 months. With runway 18 months → implied net burn ≈ $36.1K/month.

Retention-specific metrics
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR)
  - GRR = (Recurring revenue at period end from existing customers, excluding expansion) / revenue from those same customers at period start
  - Shows how much revenue you kept ignoring upsell.

- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) (very important)
  - NRR = (Revenue at period end from existing customers, including expansion and contraction, excluding new customers) / revenue from same customers at period start
  - NRR > 100% means expansion outweighs churn — strong sign.

- Customer Churn Rate (monthly or quarterly)
  - Customer churn = (Customers at start − Customers at end who remain) / Customers at start
  - Need customer counts by cohort.

- Revenue Churn Rate
  - Revenue churn = (Recurring revenue lost from churned or downgraded customers) / starting recurring revenue

- Cohort retention curve
  - Track % of revenue/customers retained by cohort month-by-month (helps identify when most churn happens).

- LTV (lifetime value) and CAC (customer acquisition cost)
