- Is $158K your net burn (expenses after revenue), or is it total cash outflow (gross expenses) before revenue offset?
- Is the $420K last-quarter revenue recurring/contracted (retainer) or one-off project revenue?
- Do you have prior-quarter or year-ago revenue figures and customer counts (needed to compute growth and retention rates)?

Once you confirm, I’ll compute exact metrics. Meanwhile, below are the metrics you’ll want, how to calculate them, what good targets look like, and a short finance narrative template you can adapt.

2) Key revenue-growth metrics (formulas + notes)
- Quarterly revenue growth (QoQ): (Revenue_Q_current − Revenue_Q_prev) / Revenue_Q_prev
- Year-over-year growth (YoY): (Revenue_Q_current − Revenue_Q_same_Q_last_year) / Revenue_Q_same_Q_last_year
- Monthly growth rate (if you track by month): (MRR_t / MRR_t-1) − 1
- ARR (if recurring): MRR × 12
- CAGR over n quarters/years: (Ending revenue / Starting revenue)^(1/n) − 1
Notes: Use quarterly for consulting/project seasonality; use rolling 12 months (TTM) for smoothing.

3) Key retention & revenue-quality metrics (formulas + interpretation)
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (Revenue from existing customers at period end, excluding expansion) / (Revenue from same customers at period start)
  - Shows how much revenue you keep if you exclude upsells. Target: >90% annually for stable services businesses.
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (Starting revenue + expansion − contraction − churn) / Starting revenue
  - Accounts for upsells/downsells. Target: ≥100% (best) — >100% means expansion offsets churn.
- Logo churn (customer count churn) = (# customers lost in period) / (# customers at period start)
  - Useful for account-based businesses.
- Revenue churn rate = (Lost revenue from churned customers) / Starting recurring revenue
- Cohort retention curve: track retention by acquisition cohort over time to identify behavior differences.
- Average Revenue per Account (ARPA) = Total revenue from customers / # customers
- CLTV (approx) = ARPA × Gross margin % / churn rate (if churn is monthly, ensure units align)
- CAC payback = CAC / (ARPA × Gross margin%) → months to recover CAC
Targets depend on stage:
