B — Key metrics, formulas and how to calculate them (with examples)

1) Revenue growth
- Quarter-over-quarter % growth = (Rev_this_quarter - Rev_prev_quarter) / Rev_prev_quarter × 100%
- Month-over-month % growth (if you have monthly data) = (M_this - M_prev)/M_prev × 100%
- Annualized growth (if comparing quarterly to same quarter prior year): YoY % = (Rev_Q - Rev_Q_last_year)/Rev_Q_last_year × 100%

Example: You gave last quarter revenue = $420K. If prior quarter was $350K, QoQ growth = (420-350)/350 = 20%.

2) Convert to MRR / ARR (for recurring businesses)
