(Include the minimal data I’ll need in parentheses — I can compute if you provide.)

1) Top-line growth
- Quarter-over-quarter (QoQ) growth = (ThisQuarterRevenue − PriorQuarterRevenue) / PriorQuarterRevenue.
  - Data needed: prior quarter revenue.
- Year-over-year (YoY) growth = (ThisQuarterRevenue − SameQuarterLastYearRevenue) / SameQuarterLastYearRevenue.

2) Runway and burn analysis
- Monthly revenue = QuarterlyRevenue / 3.
- Net burn = Gross burn − Monthly revenue (if gross burn is given).
- Runway = Cash / Net burn.
  - Data needed: confirm whether the 158K is gross or net; confirm any one-time inflows/outflows.

3) ARR / MRR (if recurring)
- ARR = LastQuarterRevenue × 4 (approx) or sum of monthly recurring revenue × 12.
- MRR = ARR / 12 or average monthly recurring revenue.
  - Data needed: how much of revenue is recurring vs one-time.

4) Retention metrics (recurring businesses)
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = Revenue from same customers at period end (excluding expansion) / Revenue from same customers at period start.
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (Revenue at end from same customers + expansion) / Revenue at start.
  - Targets: NRR >100% is excellent (expansion offsets churn). GRR ideally >85–90% depending on segment.
  - Data needed: cohort revenue at period start, churned revenue, expansion revenue.

5) Churn metrics
- Revenue churn = ChurnedRevenue / RevenueAtStartOfPeriod.
- Customer churn = CustomersLost / CustomersAtStart.
  - Data needed: customer counts and lost revenue.

6) Unit economics (if applicable)
- CAC = Total acquisition spend / New customers acquired.
- CAC payback = CAC / (Average revenue per customer per month) — months to recover CAC.
- LTV = Gross margin % × (Average revenue per customer per month × (1 / monthly churn)).
  - Data needed: marketing & sales spend, new customers, gross margin, average revenue per customer.

7) Efficiency metrics
- Burn multiple = Net burn over period / ARR net new added over same period. Lower is better (benchmark: <1.5–2 for high-quality growth).
- Gross margin, contribution margin.

Quick examples using your numbers (assume recurring revenue):
- Monthly revenue = 140K.
- If gross burn = 158K → net burn = 18K → runway ≈ 36 months.
- ARR ≈ 420K × 4 = $1.68M.

