- “Burn rate” is ambiguous: some people mean gross burn (total cash outflows / expenses) and others mean net burn (cash outflows minus cash inflows).
- Using your revenue number, these lead to very different runways:

1) If burn = gross expenses = $158k / month:
   - Monthly revenue = 420,000 / 3 = $140,000
   - Net burn = expenses − revenue = 158,000 − 140,000 = $18,000 / month
   - Implied runway = cash / net burn = 650,000 / 18,000 ≈ 36.1 months

2) If burn = net burn = $158k / month:
   - Implied runway = 650,000 / 158,000 ≈ 4.1 months

3) If runway = 18 months is correct (and cash = $650k):
   - Implied net burn = 650,000 / 18 ≈ $36,111 / month
   - With revenue = $140k / month, implied gross expenses = revenue + net burn ≈ 140,000 + 36,111 = $176,111 / month

