- If net burn = $158k:
  - Runway ≈ 4.1 months

Revenue growth metrics — what to measure and how
- Quarter-over-Quarter (QoQ) growth = (Revenue_this_quarter − Revenue_prior_quarter) / Revenue_prior_quarter
- Year-over-Year (YoY) growth (if you have seasonal effects) = (Revenue_this_quarter − Revenue_same_quarter_last_year) / Revenue_same_quarter_last_year
- CAGR (for multi-period trends)
What I need from you to compute these: prior-quarter revenue and same-quarter-last-year revenue.

Retention/ churn metrics — core definitions & formulas
- Customer (logo) churn rate = lost customers during period / number of customers at start of period
- Revenue churn (gross) = recurring revenue lost (from churned & downselling) / revenue at start of period
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR) = (Revenue at period end from same cohort, including expansions & contractions) / Revenue at period start
  - NRR > 100% means expansion offsets churn — a strong sign for SaaS/recurring businesses
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR) = (Revenue at period end from same cohort, excluding expansion) / Revenue at period start
- Example calculations I can run if you give me: number of customers at start/end, revenue lost to churn, expansion revenue, upsells, downgrades.

Benchmarks (rules of thumb)
