1) Inconsistency check (must resolve before you present runway)
- If "burn rate" = net cash burn per month, runway = cash / burn:
  - Runway = 650,000 / 158,000 ≈ 4.11 months (not 18 months).
- If runway = 18 months is correct, implied net burn = 650,000 / 18 ≈ 36,111 per month.
- With revenue last quarter = 420,000 → monthly revenue ≈ 140,000.
  - If 158K is gross operating spend and revenue reduces net burn: net burn = 158K - 140K = 18K/month → runway = 650K / 18K ≈ 36.1 months.
  - So possible interpretations:
    - You reported gross burn = 158K and revenue offsets it (net burn ≈ 18K) → runway ~36 months.
    - You intended net burn = 158K → runway ~4 months (urgent).
    - You intended runway = 18 months → net burn should be ≈36K (so maybe revenue contribution + other adjustments produce that).
Action: confirm whether the $158K is gross opex, net burn after revenue, or whether 18 months runway is calculated using projected revenue (and whether that projection is conservative).

2) Key revenue & retention metrics to compute (with formulas)
- Quarterly growth rate (QoQ):
  - QoQ % = (This Quarter Revenue - Prior Quarter Revenue) / Prior Quarter Revenue * 100
- Year-over-year growth (YoY):
  - YoY % = (This Quarter - Same Quarter Last Year) / Same Quarter Last Year * 100
- Annual Run Rate (ARR or Run-Rate Revenue):
  - ARR = Last Quarter Revenue * 4 (or MRR * 12 if monthly)
  - Example: ARR = 420K * 4 = 1.68M
- Net Burn and Runway:
  - Net burn = Total cash outflows (opex + capex) - Operating cash inflows (revenue collections)
  - Runway (months) = Cash on hand / Net burn
- Gross Revenue Retention (GRR):
  - GRR % = (Revenue at period start - churned revenue) / Revenue at period start * 100
  - Measures how much recurring revenue you keep ignoring expansion.
- Net Revenue Retention (NRR or Dollar-based NRR):
  - NRR % = (Revenue at period start + expansion + upsell - churn - contraction) / Revenue at period start * 100
  - Target: >100% is excellent for recurring businesses; >90% minimum for healthy retention.
- Monthly/Annual Churn:
  - Revenue churn % = Churned revenue in period / Revenue at period start * 100
  - Customer churn % = Customers lost / Customers at period start * 100
- Cohort retention (recommended):
  - Track % of revenue retained from each customer cohort at month 1, 3, 6, 12.
- CAC, LTV, Payback:
  - CAC = Total S&M spend / New customers acquired
  - LTV ≈ (Average revenue per customer * Gross margin %) / Customer churn rate
  - Payback (months) = CAC / Gross margin-adjusted monthly revenue per new customer
- Bookings / New ARR / Expansion ARR / Contraction ARR:
  - Report new bookings and expansion separately to show growth quality.

